# The properties an algebra's product may satisfy, in the order the number tower loses them: commutativity (the
# quaternions lose it), associativity (the octonions lose it, keeping alternativity, where any two elements generate an
# associative subalgebra), and the multiplicative norm (the sedenions lose it, where zero divisors appear). The
# alternative and flexible laws are the weakened associativity the octonions keep. These are universal equations over
# the product; the tower's losses are recorded in the algebra-tower files.
